      en: "Lake Bled (Blejsko jezero) is a world-renowned glacial lake nestled at the foot of the Julian Alps in northwestern Slovenia. Famed for its emerald-green waters, the iconic island in its center, and a medieval castle perched on a sheer cliff, it is one of Europe's most photographed destinations. Bled Island is home to the Church of the Assumption, rebuilt in the 17th century, where visitors traditionallly ring the 'wishing bell' for good fortune. Bled Castle, standing 130 meters above the lake, is documented as the oldest castle in Slovenia and offers a spectacular vantage point over the lake and the surrounding peaks. The lake measures approximately 2.1 kilometers in length and reaches a depth of 30 meters, making it a premier venue for international rowing competitions. A 6-kilometer path encircles the water, providing scenic views and easy access to the lakeside cafes. Locally, the area is famous for the 'kremna rezina' (Bled cream cake), a dessert staple since the 1950s. The unique blend of alpine nature, centuries-old history, and local traditions makes Lake Bled a must-visit year-round destination.",
